<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kashu Chaidya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kashu Chaidya was a king of the Chedi people mentioned in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a>, where a hymn praises him for generous gifts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a> to priests. He is the earliest named ruler of the Chedis, who lived south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> in the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> and later formed one of the sixteen Mahajanapadas.</p></div>
